+# Design: knowledge bundles from authored Markdown
+
+## Goal
+
+Content people write in the app (`SourceDocument` Markdown, glossary entries and
+colloquial names, see `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.source`) must become a
+`KnowledgeBundle` (`knowledge-bundle/v1`) so that publishing can run the existing bundle
+import unchanged. The conversion must be pure and deterministic: the same content
+always gives the same `bundle_digest`.
+
+## Scope
+
+Included:
+
+- A new domain module `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.authoring` that splits Markdown into
+  sections and blocks, derives stable section keys, lists sections for pickers, and
+  builds the bundle.
+- Unit tests in `backend/tests/domain/corpus/test_authoring.py`.
+
+Unchanged:
+
+- The bundle format, `bundle.py` models and validation, `bundle_digest`, the import
+  service, chunking, persistence, API and frontend. No I/O is added; the module only
+  depends on `domain.corpus.bundle`, `domain.corpus.models` and `domain.corpus.source`.
+
+## Interfaces
+
+```python
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class MarkdownSection:
+    heading: str
+    path: tuple[str, ...]      # enclosing headings incl. its own; () for the fallback section
+    ordinal: int               # 1-based, consecutive after empty sections are dropped
+    blocks: tuple[BlockRecord, ...]
+
+def split_markdown(markdown: str, *, fallback_heading: str) -> list[MarkdownSection]
+def slugify(text: str, *, max_length: int = 80) -> str
+def section_key(document_key: str, path: Sequence[str]) -> str
+def bundle_document_key(collection_key: str, document_key: str) -> str   # "<c>:<d>"
+def section_choices(collection: Collection, documents: Sequence[SourceDocument]
+                    ) -> list[tuple[str, str]]
+def build_bundle(collection: Collection, documents: Sequence[SourceDocument],
+                 glossary: Sequence[GlossaryEntry],
+                 colloquial: Sequence[ColloquialMappingRecord]) -> KnowledgeBundle
+```
+
+`Collection` is `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.models.Collection` (only `key` and `title`
+are read).
+
+## Approach
+
+**Splitting.** Lines are scanned once. A fence opens on a line starting with
+```` ``` ```` or `~~~` and closes on a line starting with the same marker; inside a fence
+nothing is a heading or a table row. ATX headings (`#` to `######`, a space, text,
+optional closing `#`s) start a new section. A heading stack keeps the path: a heading of
+level *n* pops every entry of level ≥ *n*, then pushes itself, so `path` is the chain of
+enclosing headings ending with the section's own heading. Lines before the first heading
+form a section titled `fallback_heading` with an empty path. A section whose body is only
+whitespace is dropped (its heading still encloses its children); ordinals are assigned
+afterwards, starting at 1.
+
+**Blocks.** Inside a section, consecutive lines whose left-stripped text starts with `|`
+(outside fences) form one table block; its `table_key` is `t1`, `t2`, … counted across the
+whole document. The text between tables is stripped and, when non-empty, becomes a prose
+block. Block markdown keeps the original lines (trailing whitespace trimmed).
+
+**Keys.** `slugify` NFKD-decomposes, maps `đ`/`Đ` to `d`, drops combining marks and
+non-ASCII, lowercases, joins alphanumeric runs with `-` and cuts to `max_length` at a
+hyphen boundary when possible (never leaving a trailing hyphen). `section_key` joins
+the slugified path parts with `/` after `#`; an empty path gives `#body`. Document keys
+are `"<collection key>:<document key>"` so chunk ids never collide across collections.
+If two sections of a document produce the same key (e.g. repeated headings), later ones
+get `-2`, `-3`, … appended; the same helper feeds `section_choices` and `build_bundle`
+so their keys always agree.
+
+**Bundle.** Documents become `DocumentRecord`s (kind, title, `SourceInfo(source_title,
+source_url)`, no attributes), sorted by bundle key; sections follow in that document
+order and reading order with `context_path = list(path) or [heading]` (as pharma-lab
+does). The glossary is copied as given. Colloquial mappings keep their order but lose
+section keys that are not in the bundle. The manifest carries the collection key and
+title, a fixed generator (`pharma-agent-authoring`), no source digests, no files, and the
+document and section counts. Nothing time- or random-dependent is used, so the bundle
+and its digest are deterministic.
+
+## Testing
+
+`tests/domain/corpus/test_authoring.py` covers: heading paths and nesting, fenced
+headings ignored, fallback section, empty sections dropped, table runs and document-wide
+table numbering, prose stripping, `slugify` with Vietnamese marks and length limit,
+`section_key` with empty and nested paths, `section_choices` labels and order, and
+`build_bundle` (document key format and sort, section records, glossary passthrough,
+colloquial filtering, manifest fields, passes `write_bundle` validation, same digest for
+equal input and for documents given in a different order). The full backend suite
+(`uv run pytest`) must stay green.
